cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Central thermal energy storage in a multi-feed-in district heating network (DHN-A): code and configuration package"
abstract: >
  Code and configuration package for the paper 'Central thermal energy storage at an industrial prosumer site:
  value attribution, hydraulic feasibility and foresight limits in a multi-feed-in district heating network'
  (working title, submitted to Energy). Hourly energy MILP (Pyomo, HiGHS) with a temperature-class thermal energy
  storage, an industrial waste-heat heat pump and an electrode boiler, coupled to a calibrated meshed hydraulic
  substitute network; factorial Shapley attribution, sensitivities, rolling horizon and hosting capacity. Includes a
  synthetic example data set. Operational data of the network and partner data are confidential and not included.
authors:
  - family-names: "Ruess"
    given-names: "Lukas"
    affiliation: "Institute for Energy Efficiency in Production EEP, University of Stuttgart, and Fraunhofer Institute for Manufacturing Engineering and Automation IPA"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0005-5010-3520"
license: MIT
version: "{version}"
date-released: "{date}"
keywords:
  - district heating
  - thermal energy storage
  - heat pump
  - electrode boiler
  - industrial waste heat
  - MILP
  - hydraulic network model
  - Shapley value
  - rolling horizon
